cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use smollerGraph in your work, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "smollerGraph: a small graph database, built from scratch in C++"
abstract: >-
  A small graph database built from scratch in C++20 on the YouTube series
  Building smollerGraph. It keeps a graph in fixed-size records, in 4 KiB pages
  held in memory by a buffer pool, finds nodes by name with a B+ tree, loads
  facts written as Cypher patterns, and follows relationships in either
  direction. Each step of each episode is a git tag in the repository.
authors:
  - given-names: Adrian Mircea
    family-names: Nenu
repository-code: "https://github.com/nenuadrian/smollerGraph"
url: "https://smollergraph.nenuadrian.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - graph database
  - storage engine
  - B+ tree
  - buffer pool
  - Cypher
  - C++
